The ISO list of codes could be used for the languages, but ignoring the
actual codes in favor of autonyms. IOW, if a language is on the list, it
should have a name (although all languages should have names), but not using
the code itself in the formation of that name. Many of the languages will,
of course, have names that are similar to the codes, since the codes were
apparently based on the autonyms.
stevo
